## App Store Review Skills

This project uses [apple-app-review-skills](https://github.com/cruisediary/apple-app-review-skills) — a set of 31 Claude Code skills and agents built from real Apple rejection cases across all App Store Review Guidelines sections (1–5).

### When to invoke

Invoke these skills proactively whenever the user:
- Asks about App Store submission readiness or rejection risk
- References an Apple guideline section (1.x – 5.x)
- Makes changes to permissions, privacy, IAP, UGC, layout, or metadata
- Asks why a previous submission was rejected or how to appeal

Do not wait to be explicitly asked. If code changes touch any of the areas below, suggest running the relevant audit unprompted.

### Available tools

There are two types of tools: a **slash command** (run directly by the user) and **agents** (invoked by Claude using the Agent tool).

#### Slash command

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `/appstore-detect` | Quick project inspection — reads Info.plist, checks permissions, PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy, StoreKit, and crash risk indicators. Run this first to get project context before a full audit. |

#### Agents (invoke via Agent tool)

| Agent | Scope | Triggers |
|-------|-------|----------|
| `appstore-full-audit` | Full pre-submission audit (all 31 checks) | "ready to submit", "pre-submission check", "rejection risk", any multi-area concern |
| `ipad-layout-agent` | iPad layout, Dynamic Type, safe area, orientation | Any layout or UI change, iPad-specific complaints |
| `permission-audit-agent` | NSUsageDescription strings, permission timing, scope | Adding or changing permission requests |
| `privacy-audit-agent` | Privacy policy, account deletion, ATT, PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy | Handling user data, adding analytics, account features |
| `ugc-safety-agent` | UGC report/block/filter/contact info requirements | Adding feeds, comments, chat, or user profiles |

### Routing guidance

- **Quick project inspection** → run `/appstore-detect` first to gather context
- **Single area concern** → invoke the targeted agent for that area
- **Multiple areas or pre-submission** → always invoke `appstore-full-audit`
- **Rejection email received** → identify the guideline section cited, map to the relevant agent above, fix and re-audit before resubmitting

### Priority levels in audit output

| Level | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| 🔴 CRITICAL | Guaranteed rejection — fix before submission |
| 🟠 HIGH | Very likely rejection — strongly recommended to fix |
| 🟡 MEDIUM | Possible rejection depending on reviewer — review carefully |
| 🟢 LOW | Best practice — improves approval confidence |

Address all CRITICAL and HIGH findings before submitting to App Store Connect.
